  "interpretation": "<p><strong>Comments:</strong></p>\n<p>IgG is primarily involved in immune memory and plays a major role in host defense against extracellular infections.IgG1 is the most abundant subclass of IgG species, comprises 60&ndash;65% of the total, and is predominantly responsible for the thymus-mediated immune response against proteins and polypeptide antigens.IgG1 fix complement and bind phagocyteFc&gamma; receptors well.</p>",
